id: pm-998juj
title: Bound publication weight while preserving complete runtime and metadata
description: "The published package is 40.66MB unpacked across 1,668 files (npm view @unbrained/pm-cli dist.unpackedSize/dist.fileCount, 2026.7.25). Local dist is 31MB, of which 491 .js.map files account for 20MB — tsconfig.json sets both sourceMap:true and inlineSources:true, so every map embeds the full TypeScript source (dist/sdk alone: 2.6MB JS, 1.2MB d.ts, 5.0MB maps). Those maps are already uploaded to Sentry at release time by the sentry:upload script, which reads dist/ directly, so the tarball copy is redundant for symbolication. On top of that the tarball ships both build outputs: the tsc emit (dist/cli 5.6MB, dist/core 5.4MB, dist/sdk 8.7MB) and the esbuild bundle (dist/cli-bundle 12MB, 182 chunks) that bin/exports actually resolve to. package.json also declares an unused optional peerDependency on 'typebox' — no source, package, script, or doc file references it. Duplicate check: searched install/size/tarball/sourcemap/footprint all-status. pm-oxq2 (closed) removed the nested 25MB host copy from project-scope extension installs and its own body raised 'publish a slim SDK-only package' without acting on it; pm-feecbs owns install-latency policy for the 18 external packages, not the host artifact; pm-hcrmye deliberately kept production source maps and did not examine tarball composition."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:release",distribution,ecosystem,packaging,performance
created_at: "2026-07-25T07:10:06.541Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-08T02:02:43.913Z"
author: unknown
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The published tarball no longer ships .js.map files (or ships only what symbolication provably needs), with Sentry release symbolication verified against a real captured event after the change; a documented decision records whether both the tsc emit and the esbuild bundle must ship, and any redundant output is dropped from package.json files or justified in writing; the unused typebox peer dependency is removed or a source reference is added; a size assertion in the release gates fails when unpacked size or file count regresses beyond a committed budget; npx and global install still work from a packed tarball (existing smoke:npx and package-first dogfood proofs stay green) and no runtime feature, type, or export is removed"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Cut install cost and disk footprint for every pm consumer without losing debuggability
value: "Install size is the first thing every agent, CI job, and extension workspace pays; halving it speeds cold environments, CI, and the changelog:pm reinstall path that runs on every check"
why_now: The artifact grew from the 25MB recorded in pm-oxq2 to 40.66MB with no size gate; source maps are now the single largest component and are already delivered to Sentry by a separate path
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: "Real source and Sentry-injected distributions fit unchanged ceilings while retaining all first-party metadata values, runtime bytes, SDK/CLI entrypoints and install behavior; verify Sentry release symbolication against a real captured post-change error event before closing the original acceptance criteria."
actual_result: "Lossless first-party JSON staging is implemented and verified: all 6378 archive paths, 69 parsed JSON values, 4731 runtime digests and 1578 other file bytes remain identical; 34690 bytes are saved in the paired original/candidate proof. Final current-source base 19971036 and real offline Sentry-injected 20212760 satisfy unchanged ceilings with the identical 4731-file/23334884-byte runtime closure. npm/Bun installs, Node24/26/Bun SDK clients, isolated init, npx and bunx pass. Original acceptance still requires real captured-event Sentry symbolication after this change. The CLI empty-query receipt covered unresolved issues only; an explicit resolved query returns four historical groups, latest October 7 in release 2026.10.6, whose inspected event retains seven invalid-location symbolicator diagnostics. These historical events neither establish current-candidate failure nor prove the required post-change symbolication. This broader item remains open and unclaimed; offline debug-ID injection is packaging evidence. Final connected source passes 10090 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 776 source files. Already-published main-source recovery now skips remote Sentry release metadata, commits, maps and finalization; its real Bash regression preserves tag-source upload and upload-failure propagation. Final packed-archive proof uses real offline Sentry injection, verifies both original budgets and preserves the entire checkout. Current-candidate captured-error symbolication and fresh trace visibility remain unverified."
