  - created_at: "2026-11-01T15:29:11.468Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Publication-weight tranche delivered in PR 1648 (2026-11-01): the generated error-code catalog now ships as compact rows. scripts/generate-error-code-catalog.mjs omits every derivable field (meaning sentence, class implied by exit code, shared recovery guidance, provisional stability, every-command emitters, self canonical code, empty aliases); src/sdk/generated/error-code-catalog-rows.ts expandPmErrorCodeCatalogRows (beside the generated parts, keeping src/sdk within its 120-file directory cap) restores them at load time in the original key order. Verified byte-identical: JSON.stringify(PM_ERROR_CODE_CATALOG) before and after compares equal (cmp), and tests/fixtures/contracts/full.json, docs/generated/REFUSAL_CLOSURE_CENSUS.md, agent capability surfaces and sdk/public-surface.json are unchanged. Generated catalog source fell from 190 KB to 63 KB; the catalog appears once in the tsc emit and once in each CLI bundle, so the canonical pack (npm pack --dry-run, same local dist) dropped from 20,062,612 to 19,742,574 first-party bytes (-320,038). Trigger: the PR's new SDK primitives took hosted head 2d7b03499 to 20,008,623 bytes against the unchanged 20,000,000 ceiling (main measured 19,940,474); package-artifact-gate now passes locally at 19,698,096 bytes with the ceiling unchanged. Broader acceptance (source maps, tsc-vs-bundle decision, captured-event symbolication) remains open."
    edited_at: "2026-11-01T16:06:04.820Z"
  - created_at: "2026-11-04T11:20:27.472Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Recurrence on PR #1658 (head b6a7977d1, CI run 41812019841): Gates (static) failed the unchanged 20,000,000-byte base ceiling at 20,000,673 bytes. The new weight was the PR's own documentation prose and three SDK surface acknowledgement reasons. Lossless repair, ceiling unchanged: the added prose in docs/SDK.md, docs/COMMANDS.md and docs/EXTENSION_AUTHOR_CONTRACTS.md was rewritten more tightly with every fact kept (1,167 bytes), and the three acknowledgement reasons in sdk/public-surface.json no longer repeat the symbol names their changes lists already carry (461 bytes; sdk-surface-snapshot --check still verifies 0 classified changes). Local package-artifact-gate after a clean build: distribution 19,998,947 bytes, so about 1 KB of headroom remains for the next tranche."
  - created_at: "2026-11-04T16:26:01.668Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Lossless tranche on branch fix/test-telemetry-delivery. The pm-gh1660 privacy fix adds 14,441 first-party bytes, mostly minified code emitted twice (tsc output and the two bundle variants) plus declaration JSDoc, which took the base distribution to 20,014,949 bytes, over the unchanged 20,000,000 ceiling. scripts/release/package-distribution.mjs now runs compactMarkdownTables in copyPublicationFile, beside the existing JSON compaction, on the staged publication copy only. It collapses GFM table cell padding and separator dash runs outside fenced and indented code, and refuses any row whose reparsed cells or alignment differ. Checkout files stay readable. Proof: all 199 shipped markdown files render byte-identical HTML before and after with marked (GFM). Saving: 45,276 bytes. Distribution after a clean build: 19,969,673 bytes, which leaves about 30 KB of headroom. The ceiling is unchanged and no runtime file, type or export is removed. The criterion that remains open is the decision on whether both the tsc emit (about 5.6 MB) and the bundle (about 7.0 MB) must ship."
  - created_at: "2026-11-04T18:35:40.637Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1661 review (CodeRabbit, 3 findings on compactMarkdownTables) fixed. The compaction now touches only real GFM tables: a pipe row that starts a block (first line, after a blank line or after an ATX heading), followed by a delimiter row with the same cell count, plus the pipe rows after it. Only the delimiter row has its dashes shortened, so a dash-only body row keeps its text. Lines inside fenced code and raw HTML are left alone. A fence closes only on a bare marker of the opening character that is at least as long, and a backtick info string holding a backtick opens no fence. pre, script, style and textarea blocks and HTML comments run to their closing marker, and any other HTML-opening line runs to the next blank line. Evidence: over all 184 git-tracked markdown files, marked (GFM) renders identical HTML before and after compaction, and the saving is 38,926 bytes against 38,946 for the previous version, so the package ceiling margin is unchanged in practice. tests/unit/scripts/package-distribution.spec.ts adds nine regression cases (39 tests pass).\n"
  - created_at: "2026-11-04T19:11:07.890Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1661, second review round on compactMarkdownTables (independent review agent, 5 findings). HTML start conditions 3 to 5 (processing instructions, declarations, CDATA) now run to their own closing markers. Condition 6 matches only the CommonMark block-tag list. Condition 7 needs one complete tag alone on its line, at a block start, so inline HTML in a paragraph no longer hides a later fence opener. Fence markers are found after list-item and block-quote markers. Table rows must share the header's indentation, so a row in another container ends the table. CRLF line endings are kept and no longer hide fences. A line scanner cannot model every container, for example a fence that a list item closes, so the shipped copy now goes through publicationMarkdown: the compact text is used only when marked (GFM, already a devDependency, in a script that does not ship) renders it identically to the original, and otherwise the original bytes ship. Over the 184 tracked markdown files no file falls back and the saving stays 38,926 bytes. The spec has ten more cases plus a render-check fallback case.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-11-04T20:17:23.555Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Correction to the previous comment: the packager no longer imports marked, and publicationMarkdown is gone. The release workflow runs package-distribution.mjs from a preserved copy of the reviewed release controls, which carries only their relative imports and no node_modules; tests/integration/registry-acceptance-workflow.spec.ts caught the resulting ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for marked. Container cases are now handled conservatively instead: compactMarkdownTables returns a file unchanged when any of its fences sits after indentation or a list-item or block-quote marker, because where such a fence ends depends on containers a line scanner does not model. Among the 184 tracked markdown files, none with such fences had any table savings, so the total is still 38,926 bytes. The render proof moved into the spec, where devDependencies exist: package-distribution.spec.ts renders every tracked markdown file outside .agents/pm with marked (GFM) before and after compaction, asserts identical HTML and asserts more than 30 KB saved. A future doc that the scanner would misread therefore fails CI instead of shipping changed.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-11-04T21:30:26.374Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1661, third review round on compactMarkdownTables. Cell splitting now follows GFM's backslash parity: a pipe after an even number of backslashes separates cells, including the trailing pipe, so the row from the review, alpha followed by two backslashes and a pipe, over a one-cell delimiter, is not taken for a table. CodeQL (js/bad-tag-filter) flagged the comment-end regex because it did not match --!>. This is not a sanitizer: CommonMark ends a comment block at -->. The HTML end markers are now substring predicates that follow the spec exactly, and a spec keeps a comment containing --!> raw until -->. Focused v8 coverage is 161/161 branches, the tracked-markdown render proof passes, and the distribution is 19,977,014 bytes.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-11-05T00:24:42.458Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1661, fourth CodeRabbit round, fixed. A lone HTML tag (CommonMark start condition 7) was read as raw only at the start of a file or after a blank line. It also starts a raw block after an ATX heading, a table or any other ended block; only a paragraph cannot be interrupted. For '# Page', '<custom-tag>', '# Raw heading', '| Key    |', '| ------ |' the compactor rewrote the pipe rows inside the raw block, and marked rendered different HTML. compactMarkdownTables now reads a lone tag as raw up to the next blank line wherever it appears. Inside a paragraph that only leaves a table uncompacted and never changes what renders, so no paragraph tracking is needed. New spec cases cover the heading and table-row variants. All 210 tracked markdown files outside .agents/pm still render identically under marked; the package gate reports a distribution of 19,977,367 of 20,000,000 bytes."
  - created_at: "2026-11-05T01:41:20.298Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1661, correction to the fourth-round comment: reading a lone HTML tag as raw wherever it appears could change rendering, so the claim that it only leaves a table uncompacted was wrong. A P2 PR review found the case: after a paragraph line, a lone tag is paragraph text and a fence on the next line still opens. The raw state hid that fence opener, the blank line inside the fence ended the raw state, and the table rows inside the code block were compacted. Fixed on the branch: a lone tag is raw only where it certainly starts a block, which is at the start of the file, after a blank line or ATX heading, or right after a fence or raw block ends. After any other line, a line scanner cannot tell a paragraph from a table body or a list item, so compactMarkdownTables returns the whole file unchanged, as it already does for fences inside containers. Eight paragraph, heading, table, fence and list cases render identically under marked; the previous two branch commits each failed some of them. The 210 tracked markdown files outside .agents/pm show no render difference and the same 44,941-byte saving, and the distribution is 19,977,317 of 20,000,000 bytes."
  - created_at: "2026-11-05T05:06:29.515Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1661, CodeRabbit round on 209e7234b, fixed. tableCells trimmed rows and cells with String.prototype.trim, which also strips U+00A0 and other Unicode spaces. A cell starting with a non-breaking space lost it, and the reparse check used the same trim, so it could not notice. The same trim also decided blankness, so a line holding only a non-breaking space ended a raw HTML block early, and the pipe rows after it could be compacted inside the block. GFM trims only spaces and tabs, and CommonMark calls a line blank only when it holds nothing but spaces and tabs. trimSpaces and isBlank now apply exactly those rules, and TABLE_ROW accepts only trailing spaces or tabs. Spec cases cover a leading non-breaking space in a body cell, which is kept, and a non-breaking-space line inside a div block, which stays raw. The 210 tracked markdown files outside .agents/pm still render identically under marked and save the same 44,941 bytes."
  - created_at: "2026-11-05T05:56:14.727Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Claim released after PR 1661 merged into main at 32ba98892. This PR delivered one tranche: render-equivalent markdown table compaction in scripts/release/package-distribution.mjs, saving 44,941 bytes across the 210 tracked markdown files, with the distribution at 19,979,096 of the 20,000,000-byte ceiling. Every acceptance criterion is still open: source maps out of the tarball with symbolication proven on a real captured event, the documented tsc-emit versus esbuild-bundle decision, the unused typebox peer, a committed size and file-count budget in the release gates, and green npx and dogfood proofs."
  - created_at: "2026-11-05T20:48:24.121Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "2026-11-05 release blocker, root cause and fix. Tag v2026.11.5 (6503e2736, cut by blocker_retry run 41977052960 at 06:27Z) never reached npm. Both Release runs, tag push 41980508196 and scheduled recovery dispatch 42005294363, failed at \"Sentry-injected package artifact gate\" with unpacked_size:20257274>20250000. In the same runs the base profile passed at 19,979,108 B against 20,000,000 B, with 1,799 of 1,800 first-party files.\n\nMeasured cause: sentry-cli sourcemaps inject dist/ adds exactly 358 B to every dist/**/*.js file. That is 777 files and 278,166 B, identical locally and in CI. The fixed 250,000 B sentry-injected allowance covers only about 698 files, so it stopped covering the transform once the emitted module count grew. Nothing earlier could catch this. CI runs only the base profile, and run-gates.mjs (the pre-tag local_preflight) never ran the artifact gate, although RELEASING.md said its packaging phase did. The first injected check therefore ran on an immutable tag.\n\nFix, budget version 4:\n- The sentry-injected profile is now derived. Its ceiling is the base ceiling plus max_bytes_per_injected_file (384) for each packed file matching injected_prefix dist/ and injected_suffix .js. Base content that fits the base ceiling therefore also fits after injection.\n- The gate receipt carries an injection block: base_profile, injected_file_count, max_bytes_per_injected_file and injection_allowance.\n- gate-registry local_preflight gains a forbidden-skip package-artifact step after the build. An over-budget candidate is now refused before any version commit or tag.\n- The new tests/unit/scripts/release/sentry-injection-allowance.spec.ts runs the installed @sentry/cli 3.8.2 binary offline against plain, shebang and large-module fixtures. It asserts that the delta is positive and within the allowance, so a sentry-cli upgrade that grows the snippet fails in its own PR.\n\nReplaying the exact CI packlist against the new budget gives base 19,979,108 <= 20,000,000 and injected 20,257,274 <= 20,298,368 (777 x 384 = 298,368).\n\nThe base ceiling and the file-count ceiling are unchanged. Headroom is now 20,892 B and one file, so the next weight-reduction tranche is still needed before features that add emitted modules.\n\nRecovery: release.yml exact-tag recovery copies the gate and budget from dispatch-time main into runner-temp release controls, then checks out the unpublished tag. Once this lands on main, a workflow_dispatch of release.yml for v2026.11.5 can publish the immutable tagged bytes under the reviewed policy."
  - created_at: "2026-11-05T22:35:36.324Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "PR 1672 review round 1, CodeRabbit (Major): the pre-tag preflight checked only the base packlist. Its suggestion was to run pnpm sentry:inject in local_preflight and then gate the sentry-injected profile.\n\nAccepted in intent with a safer mechanism. Injecting the checkout in place is unsafe. tsconfig.json builds incrementally (.cache/tsbuildinfo) and prepare-build-cache.mjs drops that cache only when required outputs are missing. A later pnpm build would therefore not re-emit unchanged modules, the injected snippets would stay in dist, and the next base check would fail by about 278 KB. This is the same mechanism as the 586 stale injected outputs recorded on this item on 2026-10-14.\n\nThe existing gate now accepts --simulate-injection, valid only with an injection profile. It copies dist/ to a disposable temp directory and runs the checkout's installed sentry-cli (SentryCli.getPath) on the copy. It adds each packed file's measured growth to the npm packlist, validates the injection profile and removes the copy. The receipt carries simulation.source disposable_copy, injected_file_count and added_bytes.\n\ngate-registry local_preflight now runs package-artifact (base), then package-artifact-sentry-injected (--profile=sentry-injected --simulate-injection), mirroring release.yml's base, inject, injected order before any tag exists.\n\nMeasured on the current tree: added_bytes 278166 across 777 files, the same total as CI, with injected 20258510 <= 20298368. dist is left untouched; the base profile reads the same before and after.\n\nSpecs cover the copy, the injector call, cleanup, the derived ceiling on simulated sizes, an over-ceiling failure, unchanged files, and refusal for fixed or undeclared profiles. Gate coverage is 100/100/100/100."
  - created_at: "2026-11-06T01:38:17.144Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Release recovery evidence, 2026-11-06. PR 1672 merged as a14511d0f after CI was green and Codex and CodeRabbit had no remaining findings. The operator exact-tag recovery, Release run 42137916821 (workflow_dispatch tag=v2026.11.5), copied this branch's reviewed gate and budget from main and published the unchanged v2026.11.5 tag bytes.\n\nBase and Sentry-injected profiles passed. All nine registry-acceptance jobs passed: npm, bun and npm-global on ubuntu, macos and windows. Advertise accepted release succeeded.\n\nVerified live at 01:32Z:\n- npm latest is 2026.11.5, with dist.unpackedSize 43,967,897 and fileCount 6,554.\n- GitHub Release v2026.11.5 is Latest (01:30:21Z).\n- npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.5 --version and bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.5 --version both print 2026.11.5.\n\nBlocker issue 1668 is closed with this evidence. The tranche is recorded as the closed child pm-ofllco.\n\nThis item returns to open and unclaimed. Its remaining acceptance criteria are real captured-event Sentry symbolication after the change and the next weight-reduction tranche, which is needed because headroom is one file."
  - created_at: "2026-11-07T00:18:03.784Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Next tranche landed as the closed child pm-dg68kr. Packing no longer ships the 212 dist declarations that no exported types entry reaches (266,135 B). This restores 240,986 B and 211 files of base headroom after PR 1680 exceeded both ceilings by 25,149 B and one file. Ceilings are unchanged. Decision input for the open acceptance criterion: the tsc .js emit is load-bearing, not redundant. dist/cli.js imports dist/cli/*.js, the MCP bins import dist/sdk and dist/core modules, and the ./cli export resolves to dist/cli/public.js. Dropping it would first need those entrypoints re-pointed at the esbuild bundle. Still open: Sentry symbolication proven on a real captured event after source maps left the tarball, the typebox peer, and that entrypoint decision."
  - created_at: "2026-11-07T00:18:18.219Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Correction to the previous comment: the typebox peer is not open. package.json declares only the optional @types/node peer, and the 2026-11-06 evidence comment already listed the remaining criteria without it. Still open are real captured-event Sentry symbolication after source maps left the tarball, and the tsc-emit entrypoint decision."
  - created_at: "2026-11-08T02:02:43.913Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Next tranche (2026-11-08) is the child pm-dwy8kb. Main 70c14d4a3 packed at 19,978,963 B (21,037 B headroom), and PR 1685 added about 32.5 KB of legitimate code, declarations and docs, so it failed at 20,011,469 B. Excluding the generated repository-only refusal-closure census (42,496 B) from the npm files list restores about 31 KB of headroom: the clean projection is 19,969,081 B, and the 20,000,000 B ceiling is unchanged. Each feature PR now adds roughly 30 KB across the tsc emit, both bundle chunk sets and declarations, so pruning one file per PR does not scale. The structural growth sources remain open here: CHANGELOG.md (526,799 B packed, growing with every release) and dist/sdk/public-surface.json (2,027,246 B, whose entrypoints repeat each signature per subpath and whose breaking_acknowledgements grow with every SDK change).\n"
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T21:18:48.881Z","harness:claude-code","Artifact-weight re-measurement 2026-07-25 (evening ecosystem review), measured on the freshly built dist/ tree at version 2026.7.25 (pnpm build, exit 0, \"Already up to date\").\n\ndist/ totals 40MB across 1,460 files. Of that, 526 .map files account for 28MB — roughly 70% of the whole published artifact is sourcemaps. The previously recorded baseline on this item was 40.66MB / 1,668 files with ~20MB of inlineSources sourcemaps, so total size and file count are flat-to-slightly-down while the sourcemap share has grown from about half to about seven tenths. The ratio is moving the wrong way even though the headline number is not.\n\nThat reinforces this item's existing framing rather than changing it: the sourcemaps are already uploaded to Sentry, so shipping them to every npm consumer buys nothing at install time, and they are now the dominant cost by a wide margin. The other two components this item tracks are unchanged — the artifact still carries both the tsc emit and the esbuild bundle, and the dead `typebox` peer is still declared in package.json (line 178, \"typebox\": \"*\", with a peerDependenciesMeta entry) against zero occurrences of the string typebox anywhere under src/. Confirmed by grep this pass.\n\nLive-state cross-check performed at the same time, all healthy: npm dist-tags.latest 2026.7.25 matching the local build, GitHub release v2026.7.25 present, and the last completed runs of CI, CodeQL, CodSpeed, OSSF Scorecard and Security and Script Quality all conclusion=success."
  "2026-11-05T22:54:21.153Z","harness:claude-code","Next-tranche headroom census, 2026-11-05. Measured at the PR 1672 head on the npm packlist from package-distribution.mjs, excluding the bundled runtime.\n\nCurrent state: base 19,980,344 of 20,000,000 bytes (about 19.7 KB headroom) and 1,799 of 1,800 files. Headroom is one file, so the next change that ships one more emitted module or packaged doc fails the PR base gate.\n\nMeasured candidate groups (files, bytes):\n\n| Group | Files | Bytes |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| dist tsc JavaScript under dist/sdk | 388 | 3,823,149 |\n| dist **/*.d.ts | 684 | 2,655,971 |\n| docs/*.md | 108 | 1,506,584 |\n| packages/pm-* | 85 | 387,014 |\n| .agents/skills | 27 | 77,198 |\n| plugins/ | 57 | 72,944 |\n| docs/examples | 27 | 46,155 |\n| repo-only community files (CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) | 3 | 16,234 |\n\nThe community files are referenced only by the validate well-known-files list and by docs-skills and release-readiness specs, not by any runtime package read.\n\nEach of these is a user-visible packaging decision. It belongs in its own tranche with consumer proof (npx, bunx, the SDK entrypoints and extension installs), not in a release-blocker fix."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T06:04:52.512Z","harness:codex","Compact first-party machine metadata in the publication staging copy, verify the serialized values before writing, and preserve third-party bytes. The artifact budget should reject new weight rather than grow. Real archive comparisons must retain the complete copied helper import closure; module-loading setup failures are not negative-control evidence."
  "2026-10-16T05:26:36.181Z","harness:codex","Bind package measurements to the packing pipeline, source tree or patch, and archive hash. Keep raw checkout bytes, staged compact JSON, first-party distribution size, and bundled-runtime totals distinct; only a controlled same-candidate comparison proves an exclusion delta."
